; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Shape Maker
; CATEGORY: Shapes & Polygons
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     input, readlist, polygon, validation
; SUMMARY:  Asks how many sides and how long they are, then draws that polygon in the middle of the screen.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The program asks you two questions in the command center:
;   how many sides, and how long each side should be. Then it
;   draws your shape, centered, in a new color. It keeps going
;   so you can stack shapes on top of each other.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and answer in the command center (type a number
;   and press Enter). Type quit at any question to finish.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * READLIST waits for the user to type a line
;   * checking an answer with NUMBERP before using it
;   * a procedure that asks again until the answer makes sense
;   * a little trigonometry to put a shape's center in the middle
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Draw 3, 4, 5 and 6 sides all with length 150.
;   * Try 100 sides of length 5. What does it look like?
;   * Change the color list in DRAWCENTERED.
; ============================================================

; Ask a question and give back a whole number between low and high.
; If the answer is not a number, or is out of range, say so and ask
; again. A typed "quit" comes back as the word quit.
to asknumber :question :low :high
  print :question
  localmake "answer readlist
  if emptyp :answer [output asknumber :question :low :high]
  localmake "word first :answer
  if equalp lowercase :word "quit [output "quit]
  if not numberp :word [
    print (sentence [Please type a number, like] :low)
    output asknumber :question :low :high
  ]
  if or :word < :low :word > :high [
    print (sentence [Choose a number from] :low [to] :high)
    output asknumber :question :low :high
  ]
  output int :word
end

; Draw a regular polygon with its center at (0, 0).
; The "apothem" is the distance from the center to the middle of
; a side. We start in the middle of the bottom side's left half,
; so the shape ends up balanced round the center of the screen.
to drawcentered :sides :length
  localmake "apothem :length / (2 * tan 180 / :sides)
  penup
  setxy minus :length / 2 minus :apothem
  setheading 90
  pendown
  setpencolor item 1 + remainder :shapes 8 [1 4 2 13 14 5 10 8]
  repeat :sides [forward :length left 360 / :sides]
  make "shapes :shapes + 1
end

to shapemaker
  make "shapes 0
  forever [
    localmake "sides asknumber [How many sides? Pick 3 to 30.] 3 30
    if equalp :sides "quit [print [Goodbye!] stop]
    localmake "length asknumber [How long is each side? Pick 5 to 250.] 5 250
    if equalp :length "quit [print [Goodbye!] stop]
    ; a big shape with many sides would not fit on the screen
    ifelse (:length * :sides) > 1700 [
      print [That shape is too big for the screen. Try a shorter side.]
    ] [
      drawcentered :sides :length
      print (sentence [Here is your shape with] :sides [sides.])
    ]
  ]
end

clearscreen
setpensize 3
hideturtle
print [Welcome to the Shape Maker. Type quit to stop.]
shapemaker
